- Assertions: Counterexamples (assertMutExRolesHeldInEmergency, assertPreEmergencyDelegationPersists)
- Predicates: Unsatisfiable (PreEmergencyDelegationPersistsVerification_Positive, EmergencyDelegationWithLateExpiryVerification_Negative, SelfDelegationVerification_Negative, DelegatorNotAssignedRoleVerification_Negative, ClearanceMismatchVerification_Negative)
- Instances: Mixed (some meaningful, some missing required coverage)
- Vacuity: Possible (assertPreEmergencyDelegationPersists vacuously not tested; negative unsats due to enforced facts)
- Overall: Incomplete

=== CONVERGENCE_RECOMMENDATION ===
Status: FALSE
Reasoning: Further refinements are required. Counterexamples and unsatisfiable predicates indicate incomplete coverage and vacuity in positive Emergency and delegation persistence scenarios. User requests that, for verification purposes, every relevant run/check must always include at least one Emergency state, a mutually exclusive role pair, and a delegation spanning Emergency mode. Additional scenario construction and stronger predicates are needed before convergence.

=== ALLOY_MODEL_IMPROVEMENTS ===
1. Strengthen EmergencyScenario_Positive and all related predicates to enforce that, during Emergency mode, at least one user holds both roles in a mutually exclusive pair:
   - Add to EmergencyScenario_Positive:
     ```
