3. Clarify that negative scenario tests (e.g., self-delegation, delegator not assigned role) rely on facts and do not require explicit scenario construction; instead, ensure facts are sufficient.
4. Strengthen R4.2b to clarify that delegations assigned before Emergency are not automatically revoked at Emergency exit and must remain active until their explicit expiry or explicit revocation.
5. In the "Newly Discovered Requirement Gaps" section, add that for each positive test, the scenario preconditions (e.g., Emergency present, delegation present) must always be satisfied in verification runs.

=== USER QUESTIONS ===
1. For verification purposes, is it acceptable to require that every run/check command for Emergency-related assertions/scenarios must always construct at least one Emergency state, a mutually exclusive role pair, and a user holding both roles during Emergency? (User: Yes.)
2. Should delegation scenarios always include at least one delegation spanning Emergency mode for verification, or is it sufficient to test such persistence only in separate, dedicated runs? (User: For verification purposes, always include at least one delegation spanning Emergency mode.)
