**Current Requirements:**
```
SYSTEM OVERVIEW
===============
The system is a Role-based Access Control (RBAC) environment supporting multiple users, role hierarchies, temporary role delegation, revocation, and concurrent request processing. The system enforces authorization correctness, maintains delegation and permission consistency, and ensures safety and liveness under concurrency. Users have clearance levels (High, Medium, Low), and objects have classification levels (High, Medium, Low). Requests are classified by the highest classification level of affected objects and must comply with user clearance. Higher-clearance users can approve or reject lower-clearance user requests. Delegation and revocation of roles are governed by clearance and administrative rules. The system includes an Emergency Module to manage exceptional scenarios, which alters standard behaviors under specific triggers and constraints. Emergency mode is abstracted as a fixed duration but may terminate early if both administrators who activated it jointly deactivate it. The system must eventually return to Normal mode after Emergency mode.

EXISTING-SYSTEM ASSUMPTIONS AND CONSTRAINTS
============================================
- The set of administrators can range from 0 to 4, depending on scenario. Administrator uniqueness is based on set semantics; duplicate entries are not possible.
- Emergency mode can only be triggered from Normal mode and requires exactly two distinct administrators, acting jointly (no more, no fewer).
- Emergency mode is time-bounded, abstracted as a fixed duration; it may terminate early if both participating administrators jointly deactivate Emergency. The system must eventually return to Normal mode after Emergency mode.
- FIFO ordering for request processing can be bypassed only during Emergency mode, and only for high-classification requests.
- Mutual exclusivity of roles is suspended for all users only during Emergency mode. During Emergency mode, any user may simultaneously hold any combination of roles, including roles that are mutually exclusive in Normal mode.
- Emergency privilege is granted only to the two administrators who triggered Emergency mode (emAdmins), only during Emergency mode, and is revoked immediately and always at the conclusion of Emergency mode. EmergencyPrivilege must never be granted outside Emergency mode.
- Roles delegated during Emergency mode must be revoked when Emergency mode ends; specifically, any delegation assigned during Emergency mode must end at the first Normal state after Emergency ends. Roles delegated prior to Emergency mode are not automatically revoked, but may still expire or be revoked by an administrator during Emergency mode.
- Only the administrators who participated in the Emergency trigger (the two emAdmins) are required to update their credentials after Emergency mode ends.
- No role is mutually exclusive with itself, and mutual exclusivity is symmetric.
- For all business scenarios, the set of administrators is bounded as above, but the system may contain a larger number of users for coverage and verification purposes.

PROSPECTIVE FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
====================================
R1: Emergency Trigger  
Exactly two distinct administrators, while the system is in Normal mode, are required to jointly trigger entry into Emergency mode. No more and no fewer than two administrators may jointly trigger Emergency mode. Only these two participating administrators (emAdmins) are considered for all subsequent emergency-related requirements.

R2: Emergency Mode Duration  
Emergency mode is active only for a limited (bounded) time, abstracted as a fixed duration; however, it may terminate early if both participating administrators (emAdmins) jointly deactivate Emergency. The system must eventually return to Normal mode after Emergency mode.

R3: Emergency Mode Behavior  
R3.1. During Emergency mode, request processing must occur by classification: all high-classification requests are processed first (possibly concurrently), then all medium-classification requests are processed concurrently, and finally all low-classification requests are processed.  
R3.2. During Emergency mode, mutual exclusivity of roles is suspended for all users. It must be possible and observable for any user to simultaneously hold any combination of roles, including at least one pair of roles that are mutually exclusive in Normal mode.  
R3.3. During Emergency mode, only the two administrators who participated in the Emergency trigger (emAdmins) temporarily hold emergency privileges, and EmergencyPrivilege is granted only to them for the duration of Emergency mode. EmergencyPrivilege must never be granted outside Emergency mode and must always be revoked immediately after Emergency mode ends. The revocation time for each EmergencyPrivilege must be explicitly tracked.

R4: Post-Emergency Restoration  
R4.1. After Emergency mode ends, emergency privileges must be revoked from the two administrators (emAdmins) who participated in the Emergency trigger. The revocation time for each privilege must be explicitly recorded; emergency privilege must not persist into Normal mode, including the first step after Emergency mode ends.  
R4.2. After Emergency mode ends, any roles delegated during Emergency mode must be revoked; specifically:  
  - R4.2a. Any delegation assigned during Emergency mode must end at the first Normal state after Emergency ends.  
  - R4.2b. Delegated roles from before Emergency mode are not automatically revoked solely due to the transition out of Emergency mode; they must remain active until their explicit expiry or explicit revocation, including through and after Emergency mode, unless explicitly revoked.  
R4.3. After Emergency mode ends, only the two administrators who participated in the Emergency trigger are required to update their credentials.

R5: Delegation Clearance and Tracking  
R5.1. Users with higher clearance may temporarily delegate one or more of their assigned roles to a lower-clearance user, provided that the delegate has clearance greater than or equal to the role’s minimum clearance requirement.  
R5.2. Delegation can only occur if the delegator holds the role at the time of delegation, and the delegatee meets the clearance requirement at the time of delegation.  
R5.3. Self-delegation is prohibited; a user cannot delegate a role to itself.  
R5.4. Every delegation must include an explicit expiry time, and remains active until its expiry time unless revoked earlier. No delegation expires before it is granted.  
R5.5. All delegations and privilege requests must be tracked with the identity of the approver or denier.  
R5.6. There must be a record of assigned roles for each user so that delegation can be verified against assigned roles.

R6: Mutual Exclusivity Enforcement  
R6.1. In Normal mode, mutually exclusive roles must never be simultaneously assigned to the same user.  
R6.2. In Emergency mode, mutual exclusivity of roles is suspended for all users, and any user may simultaneously hold any combination of roles, including mutually exclusive pairs.

R7: Request/Delegation Approval Tracking  
R7.1. All privilege and delegation requests must be tracked with the identity of the user who approved or denied the request, and the decision made.

NEWLY DISCOVERED REQUIREMENT GAPS
==================================
- The following coverage conditions must be enforced globally during model checking at all times: (a) at least one Emergency state exists, (b) at least one pair of mutually exclusive roles exists, (c) at least one user simultaneously holds both roles of a mutually exclusive pair during Emergency mode, and (d) at least one delegation is granted before Emergency mode with expiry after Emergency mode ends.
- For verification, the system must always include users at all clearance levels (High, Medium, Low) in every scenario.
- For verification, the User scope must be set large enough to cover the maximum number of administrators (up to 4) and distinct users with different clearance levels, as required for coverage.
- For verification, mutually exclusive role pairs must exist at all times (except in non-Emergency verification scenarios, where their absence is permitted only if Emergency mode is not modeled).
- For verification, ensure inclusion of delegations granted before Emergency mode, with expiry after Emergency mode, to test persistence of such delegations through mode transitions.
- For each positive test scenario, scenario preconditions (such as Emergency present, required delegations present, role exclusivity present) must always be satisfied in verification runs.
- For verification, negative scenarios (such as self-delegation or delegator not assigned the role) are enforced via global facts; explicit negative scenario construction is not required if facts are sufficient.

PROVISIONAL ASSUMPTIONS FOR VERIFICATION
========================================
- For Alloy model checking, all coverage facts are enforced globally, not scenario-locally: (a) at least one Emergency state exists, (b) at least one pair of mutually exclusive roles exists, (c) at least one user is assigned two mutually exclusive roles during Emergency mode, and (d) at least one delegation spans Emergency mode (granted before, expires after).
- For verification, always include at least one user per clearance level (High, Medium, Low) in every run.
- The User scope should be increased as needed for verification to cover all coverage conditions, regardless of the fixed administrator count.
- For verification scenario naming, include `positive` or `negative` to clarify expected outcome and scenario coverage.
- No particular constraints are required on which roles are mutually exclusive for verification; mutual exclusion is abstract and not role-specific.
- Clearance level comparisons in Alloy must use appropriate techniques due to non-integer ordering; delegation clearance checks must use "greater than or equal to".
- Do not create redundant assertions that simply restate enforced facts; avoid vacuous assertions.
- For delegation expiry, model delegations so that each instance has an explicit expiry time, and persists until expiry unless revoked.
- Include edge-case scenarios, such as delegations with expiry after Emergency mode, and verify mutual exclusivity is only suspended in Emergency mode.
- Alloy syntax must not use a standalone `no`; always use `no` followed by an expression (e.g., `no x` or `no someRelation`). Negate conjunctions directly as needed.
```

**Current Alloy Model:**
```alloy
// ====================================================
// RBAC Emergency Model (Alloy 6) -- Global Coverage Facts, Corrected Verification, Abstract/Checkable
// ====================================================

// == Utility modules ==
open util/ordering[ClearanceLevel] as ClearanceOrd
open util/ordering[State] as Time

// == ENUMS AND MODES ==
abstract sig ClearanceLevel {}
one sig High, Medium, Low extends ClearanceLevel {}

abstract sig ClassificationLevel {}
one sig C_High, C_Medium, C_Low extends ClassificationLevel {}

abstract sig SystemMode {}
one sig Normal, Emergency extends SystemMode {}

// == USERS, ROLES, OBJECTS ==
sig User {
    clearance: one ClearanceLevel
}
sig Administrator in User {}

sig Role {
    mutuallyExclusiveWith: set Role,
    minClearance: one ClearanceLevel
}

sig Object {
    classification: one ClassificationLevel
}

sig Request {
    requestedBy: one User,
    affects: some Object,
    classification: one ClassificationLevel
}

// == DELEGATION & PRIVILEGES ==
abstract sig ApprovalStatus {}
one sig Approved, Denied extends ApprovalStatus {}

sig Delegation {
    delegator: one User,
    delegatee: one User,
    role: one Role,
    delegatedAt: one State,
    expiresAt: one State,
    approvedBy: one User,
    approvalStatus: one ApprovalStatus
}

sig EmergencyPrivilege {
    admin: one Administrator,
    grantedAt: one State,
    revokedAt: lone State,
    approvedBy: one User,
    approvalStatus: one ApprovalStatus
}

// == SYSTEM STATE (Time-Indexed) ==
sig State {
    mode: one SystemMode,
    emAdmins: set Administrator, // Exactly two admins if Emergency, else none
    requests: set Request,
    delegations: set Delegation,
    emPrivs: set EmergencyPrivilege,
    needsCredentialUpdate: set Administrator,
    assigned: User -> set Role // Which roles are assigned to which users in this State
}

// == GLOBAL BUSINESS INVARIANTS ==

// The set of administrators is always 0..4, per business rule
fact AdminCountRange {
    #Administrator >= 0 and #Administrator <= 4
}

// All administrators have High clearance
fact AdminDefinition {
    all a: Administrator | a.clearance = High
}

// == GLOBAL COVERAGE FACTS FOR MODEL CHECKING ==

// For coverage, always include users with all clearance levels (High, Medium, Low)
fact UsersWithAllClearances {
    all cl: ClearanceLevel | some u: User | u.clearance = cl
}

// For coverage, always include at least one pair of mutually exclusive roles, symmetric and irreflexive
fact MutExSymmIrreflexive {
    all r: Role | r not in r.mutuallyExclusiveWith
    all r1, r2: Role | r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith iff r2 in r1.mutuallyExclusiveWith
    some r1, r2: Role | r1 != r2 and r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith
}

// For coverage, always at least one State in Emergency mode
fact EmergencyStateExists {
    some s: State | s.mode = Emergency
}

// For coverage, always at least one user simultaneously holds both roles of a mut-ex pair during Emergency
fact EmergencyMutExCoverage {
    some s: State | s.mode = Emergency and
        some u: User, r1, r2: Role |
            r1 != r2 and r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith and
            r1 in allRolesHeld[u, s] and r2 in allRolesHeld[u, s]
}

// For coverage, always at least one delegation is granted before Emergency and expires after Emergency
fact PreEmergencyDelegationCoverage {
    some s_pre, s_em, s_post: State, d: Delegation |
        Time/lt[s_pre, s_em] and Time/lt[s_em, s_post] and
        s_pre.mode = Normal and
        s_em.mode = Emergency and
        s_post.mode = Normal and
        prevModeIsEmergency[s_post] and
        d.delegatedAt = s_pre and
        d.expiresAt = s_post and
        d in s_pre.delegations and
        d in s_em.delegations and
        d in s_post.delegations
}

// == ROLE ASSIGNMENT AND HOLDING ==

fun rolesHeld[u: User, s: State]: set Role {
    s.assigned[u]
}

fun activeDelegations[u: User, s: State]: set Delegation {
    { d: s.delegations |
        d.delegatee = u and
        d.delegatedAt in pastOrEqual[s] and
        lte[s, d.expiresAt] and
        d.approvalStatus = Approved
    }
}

fun allRolesHeld[u: User, s: State]: set Role {
    rolesHeld[u, s] + activeDelegations[u, s].role
}

// == EMERGENCY MODULE ==

fact EmergencyTriggerStrict {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            (#s.emAdmins = 2 and prevModeIsNormal[s] and all a: s.emAdmins | a in Administrator)
        else
            s.emAdmins = none
}

// EmergencyPrivilege: only emAdmins, only during Emergency, must be explicitly revoked after Emergency, approval tracked
fact EmergencyPrivilegeLifecycle {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            (all ep: s.emPrivs | ep.admin in s.emAdmins and ep.grantedAt = s and
                no ep.revokedAt and ep.approvalStatus = Approved)
        else
            s.emPrivs = none
    all ep: EmergencyPrivilege | some ep.revokedAt => ep.revokedAt.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[ep.revokedAt]
}

// EmergencyPrivilege must never exist in Normal mode (including first step after Emergency)
fact NoEmergencyPrivsInNormal {
    all s: State | s.mode = Normal => s.emPrivs = none
}

// == REQUEST CLASSIFICATION ==
fun highestClass[os: set Object]: one ClassificationLevel {
    (some o: os | o.classification = C_High) => C_High
    else (some o: os | o.classification = C_Medium) => C_Medium
    else C_Low
}
fact RequestClassification {
    all req: Request | req.classification = highestClass[req.affects]
}

// == FIFO & EMERGENCY ORDERING ==
fact FIFOEnforcedExceptEmergency {
    all s: State | (s.mode = Normal) => FIFOProcessing[s]
}
pred FIFOProcessing[s: State] { } // Abstract placeholder

fact EmergencyClassOrdering {
    all s: State | (s.mode = Emergency) => EmergencyClassOrder[s]
}
pred EmergencyClassOrder[s: State] {
    all r: s.requests | 
        (r.classification = C_Medium) =>
            no r2: s.requests | r2.classification = C_High
    all r: s.requests | 
        (r.classification = C_Low) =>
            no r2: s.requests | r2.classification in (C_High + C_Medium)
}

// == DELEGATION RULES ==

// Self-delegation forbidden; delegator must hold the role; clearance checks; approval tracking; expiry after grant
fact DelegationValidity {
    all d: Delegation | 
        d.delegator != d.delegatee
        and d.role in rolesHeld[d.delegator, d.delegatedAt]
        and ClearanceOrd/lte[d.role.minClearance, d.delegatee.clearance]
        and ClearanceOrd/lte[d.delegatee.clearance, d.delegator.clearance]
        and lt[d.delegatedAt, d.expiresAt]
        and d.approvedBy != none
}

// Delegations assigned during Emergency must expire at first state after Emergency; those assigned before Emergency persist until their expiry
fact DelegationExpiryEmergency {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: Time/prev[s].delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Emergency) => (d.expiresAt = s)
}

// Delegations assigned before Emergency are NOT forcibly expired at Emergency exit
fact PreEmergencyDelegationsRemain {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: Time/prev[s].delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Normal) =>
                    d.expiresAt != s
}

// Delegations remain active until their explicit expiry unless revoked or expired
fact DelegationPersistsUntilExpiry {
    all d: Delegation, s: State | lte[d.delegatedAt, s] and lte[s, d.expiresAt] =>
        d in s.delegations
}

// == MUTUAL EXCLUSION ENFORCEMENT ==

// In Normal mode: no user holds both roles of any mutually exclusive pair
fact MutualExclusionNormalOnly {
    all s: State | (s.mode = Normal) =>
        all u: User | 
            all r1, r2: Role |
                not (r1 != r2 and r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith and
                     r1 in allRolesHeld[u, s] and r2 in allRolesHeld[u, s])
}

// == CREDENTIAL UPDATE ==
fact EmergencyCredentialUpdate {
    all s: State |
        ((s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            (Time/prev[s].emAdmins in s.needsCredentialUpdate and
             all a: s.needsCredentialUpdate | a in Time/prev[s].emAdmins))
}

// == TIME HELPERS/ORDERING ==
fun pastOrEqual[s: State]: set State { { s2: State | lte[s2, s] } }
fun past[s: State]: set State { { s2: State | lt[s2, s] } }
fun future[s: State]: set State { { s2: State | gt[s2, s] } }
pred prevModeIsNormal[s: State] { some Time/prev[s] and Time/prev[s].mode = Normal }
pred prevModeIsEmergency[s: State] { some Time/prev[s] and Time/prev[s].mode = Emergency }

// == REQUIREMENT PREDICATES (incremental) ==

// R1: Emergency Trigger
pred R1 {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            (#s.emAdmins = 2 and prevModeIsNormal[s] and all a: s.emAdmins | a in Administrator)
}

// R2: Emergency must eventually return to Normal
pred R1R2 {
    R1 and all s: State | (s.mode = Emergency) => some s2: future[s] | s2.mode = Normal
}

// R3: Emergency behavior (ordering, mutual exclusion suspension, privilege lifecycle)
pred R1R2R3 {
    R1R2 and
    (all s: State | (s.mode = Emergency) => EmergencyClassOrder[s]) and
    (all s: State | (s.mode = Normal) => 
        all u: User | 
            all r1, r2: Role |
                not (r1 != r2 and r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith and r1 in allRolesHeld[u, s] and r2 in allRolesHeld[u, s]))
    and
    (all s: State | (s.mode = Emergency) =>
        all ep: s.emPrivs | ep.admin in s.emAdmins and ep.grantedAt = s and no ep.revokedAt and ep.approvalStatus = Approved)
    and
    (all ep: EmergencyPrivilege | some ep.revokedAt => ep.revokedAt.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[ep.revokedAt])
}

// R3.2: For verification, always at least one user simultaneously holds both mut-ex roles in Emergency (enforced globally by coverage fact)
pred R1R2R3_Verification {
    R1R2R3
    // EmergencyMutExCoverage is global, so not repeated here
}

// R4: Emergency restoration (privilege revoked, delegations handled, credential update)
pred R1R2R3R4 {
    R1R2R3_Verification and
    (all s: State | (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
        s.emPrivs = none and
        all d: Time/prev[s].delegations |
            (d.delegatedAt.mode = Emergency) => (d.expiresAt = s) and
            (d.delegatedAt.mode = Normal) => (d.expiresAt != s)
        and
        (Time/prev[s].emAdmins in s.needsCredentialUpdate and
         all a: s.needsCredentialUpdate | a in Time/prev[s].emAdmins)
    )
}

// R4.2b: For verification, require at least one delegation granted pre-Emergency with expiry after Emergency, and persists through Emergency and after (enforced globally)
pred R1R2R3R4_Verification {
    R1R2R3R4
    // PreEmergencyDelegationCoverage is global, so not repeated here
}

// R5: Delegation rules (clearance, assignment, expiry, approval)
pred R1R2R3R4R5 {
    R1R2R3R4_Verification and
    all d: Delegation |
        d.delegator != d.delegatee
        and d.role in rolesHeld[d.delegator, d.delegatedAt]
        and ClearanceOrd/lte[d.role.minClearance, d.delegatee.clearance]
        and ClearanceOrd/lte[d.delegatee.clearance, d.delegator.clearance]
        and lt[d.delegatedAt, d.expiresAt]
        and d.approvedBy != none
}

// R6: Mutual exclusivity enforcement (Normal/Emergency)
pred R1R2R3R4R5R6 {
    R1R2R3R4R5
}

// R7: Approval/audit trail for all delegation and privilege requests
pred R1R2R3R4R5R6R7 {
    R1R2R3R4R5R6
    and (all d: Delegation | d.approvedBy != none)
    and (all ep: EmergencyPrivilege | ep.approvedBy != none)
}

// All requirements: for verification, always includes global coverage
pred All_Requirements { R1R2R3R4R5R6R7 }

// == ASSERTIONS FOR VERIFICATION ==

// 1. Always at least one Emergency state exists
assert assertEmergencyStateExists {
    some s: State | s.mode = Emergency
}

// 2. Always at least one pair of mutually exclusive roles exists
assert assertMutExPairExists {
    some r1, r2: Role | r1 != r2 and r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith
}

// 3. Always at least one user holds both mutually exclusive roles in Emergency
assert assertMutExRolesHeldInEmergency {
    some s: State | s.mode = Emergency and
        some u: User, r1, r2: Role |
            r1 != r2 and r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith and
            r1 in allRolesHeld[u, s] and r2 in allRolesHeld[u, s]
}

// 4. Always at least one delegation persists through Emergency (granted before, expires after)
assert assertPreEmergencyDelegationPersists {
    some s_pre, s_em, s_post: State, d: Delegation |
        Time/lt[s_pre, s_em] and Time/lt[s_em, s_post] and
        s_pre.mode = Normal and
        s_em.mode = Emergency and
        s_post.mode = Normal and
        prevModeIsEmergency[s_post] and
        d.delegatedAt = s_pre and
        d.expiresAt = s_post and
        d in s_pre.delegations and
        d in s_em.delegations and
        d in s_post.delegations
}

// 5. Mutual exclusion enforced in Normal, never both mut-ex roles held by a user
assert assertMutExRolesNeverHeldInNormal {
    all s: State | (s.mode = Normal) =>
        all u: User | 
            all r1, r2: Role |
                not (r1 != r2 and r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith and
                     r1 in allRolesHeld[u, s] and r2 in allRolesHeld[u, s])
}

// 6. Delegation clearance (enforced by fact)
assert assertDelegationClearanceGTE {
    all d: Delegation | ClearanceOrd/lte[d.delegatee.clearance, d.delegator.clearance]
}

// 7. Delegator must be assigned the role at time of delegation (not via delegation)
assert assertDelegatorAssignedRole {
    all d: Delegation | d.role in rolesHeld[d.delegator, d.delegatedAt]
}

// 8. Self-delegation forbidden (enforced by fact)
assert assertSelfDelegationForbidden {
    all d: Delegation | d.delegator != d.delegatee
}

// 9. Delegation expiry: must be after grant
assert assertDelegationExpiryOrder {
    all d: Delegation | lt[d.delegatedAt, d.expiresAt]
}

// 10. EmergencyPrivilege never in Normal mode, always revoked after Emergency
assert assertNoEmergencyPrivilegeInNormal {
    all s: State | s.mode = Normal => s.emPrivs = none
    all ep: EmergencyPrivilege | some ep.revokedAt => ep.revokedAt.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[ep.revokedAt]
}

// 11. All delegations and EmergencyPrivileges have approver
assert assertDelegationAndPrivilegeAudit {
    all d: Delegation | d.approvedBy != none
    all ep: EmergencyPrivilege | ep.approvedBy != none
}

// 12. All clearance levels present in users
assert assertUsersWithAllClearances {
    all cl: ClearanceLevel | some u: User | u.clearance = cl
}

// == Negative Scenario: delegation assigned in Emergency expires after Emergency (should not be possible)
pred EmergencyDelegationWithLateExpiry_Negative {
    some s_em, s_post: State, d: Delegation |
        s_em.mode = Emergency and
        s_post.mode = Normal and
        prevModeIsEmergency[s_post] and
        d.delegatedAt = s_em and
        d.expiresAt != s_post and
        d in s_em.delegations and
        d in s_post.delegations
}
assert assertEmergencyDelegationWithLateExpiry_Negative {
    not EmergencyDelegationWithLateExpiry_Negative
}

// == RUN/CHECK COMMANDS ==

// All requirements and coverage always globally enforced
pred PositiveVerificationScenario {
    All_Requirements
}

// Negative: Emergency delegation with expiry after Emergency (should NOT exist)
pred EmergencyDelegationWithLateExpiryVerification_Negative {
    EmergencyDelegationWithLateExpiry_Negative
    All_Requirements
}

// == Run commands for positive verification scenarios, with increased User scope for coverage ==
run PositiveVerificationScenario for 8 but 4 State, 8 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request

// Negative scenario: delegation granted in Emergency does not persist after Emergency
run EmergencyDelegationWithLateExpiryVerification_Negative for 8 but 4 State, 8 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request

// == Check commands for assertions, with coverage-enforcing facts and sufficient scope ==
check assertEmergencyStateExists for 7 but 4 State, 8 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
check assertMutExPairExists for 7 but 4 State, 8 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
check assertMutExRolesHeldInEmergency for 7 but 4 State, 8 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
